                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-10T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 10,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 12—11:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. My 43, February 10, 11 a.m. Ministry of Communications yesterday sent a
                    strong telegram to the Chinese delegates opposing alleged French project of
                    international control of wireless in China or any interference with Federal
                    contract also declaring Chinese Government’s support policy equal opportunity
                    and repudiation monopolistic discriminatory clauses British and Japanese
                    wireless contracts. Ministry Communications requests that American delegates
                    consent to confer privately with Chinese delegate on the subject of wireless
                    communications with a view to joint action in the face of British, Japanese and
                    French policies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
